  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🧑 D&D Human Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Human names for the Forgotten Realms, in the styles of the Sword Coast, the north and Damara."
    },
    "intro": "Humans are the most varied people in D&D, and in the Forgotten Realms their names depend on where they come from. The fifth-edition Player's Handbook lists nine human ethnic groups of Faerûn, each with its own naming style. This **D&D human name generator** covers three of the most common in Sword Coast adventures: Chondathan (also used by Tethyrians), Illuskan and Damaran.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Human names in the Forgotten Realms",
        "content": "<p>The Player's Handbook (2014) names nine human groups in Faerûn: Calishite, Chondathan, Damaran, Illuskan, Mulan, Rashemi, Shou, Tethyrian and Turami. Each has its own names, many loosely inspired by real-world languages.</p><p>This generator covers three:</p><ul><li><strong>Chondathan and Tethyrian:</strong> the most common names along the Sword Coast, in cities like Baldur's Gate and Waterdeep. They sound like English and Western European names, slightly altered.</li><li><strong>Illuskan:</strong> the seafaring people of the cold northern Sword Coast, around Luskan. Their names have a Norse feel and their surnames often come from the sea.</li><li><strong>Damaran:</strong> from Damara, in the Bloodstone Lands of north-eastern Faerûn. Their names have a Slavic sound.</li></ul><p>All the names here are new, so you won't share one with an example from the book.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Choosing a name for your human",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Start with where they grew up.</strong> A fisherman from Luskan and a noble from Waterdeep shouldn't sound alike.</li><li><strong>Use the surname for backstory.</strong> Illuskan sea names (Saltbeard, Tidebreaker) say \"sailor family\" at once.</li><li><strong>Mix for travellers.</strong> A human raised in a port city might have a Chondathan first name and an Illuskan surname.</li></ul><p>For the other peoples of the Realms, see the <a href=\"../categories/dnd-names.html\">D&amp;D name generators</a>, or try the <a href=\"baldurs-gate-3-name-generator.html\">Baldur's Gate 3 Name Generator</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What are the human ethnicities in the Forgotten Realms?",
        "answer": "The 2014 Player's Handbook lists nine: Calishite, Chondathan, Damaran, Illuskan, Mulan, Rashemi, Shou, Tethyrian and Turami."
      },
      {
        "question": "What names do humans use in Baldur's Gate?",
        "answer": "Mostly Chondathan and Tethyrian names, the common style of the Sword Coast's cities, with Illuskan names among people from the north."
      },
      {
        "question": "Why only three styles?",
        "answer": "They're the ones you'll meet most in Sword Coast adventures. The others are tied closely to real-world cultures, and deserve more care than a quick generator can give."
      }
